// The last escalatory incident here - reserves called up and moved to the frontier - is the
// one that is no longer really an incident: it is the week before a war, and it is priced
// accordingly, with the largest grievance and the largest rally in the table.
//
// The three below it calm a crisis instead of deepening it, and they are not decoration.
// Every review is another chance for a rivalry to get worse, and a table of incidents that
// only escalates turns every rivalry into a war eventually. Great powers do hold summits,
// sign arms control and let mediators broker ceasefires - and a game about 2024 needs a
// world where that is possible, or the only diplomacy that matters is the ultimatum.
